{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1137648-favorite-old-scarred-lands-books","id":1137648,"title":"Favorite Old Scarred Lands Books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-05T05:29:46-07:00","id":1137648,"title":"Favorite Old Scarred Lands Books","content":"So what were your favorite old Scarred Lands books?<br /> <br /> Mine were:<br /> <br /> 1. Strange Lands, closely followed by...<br /> 2. Echoes of the Past<br /> 3. Blood Bayou<br /> 4. Termana (even though I run most of my games in Ghelspad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T11:50:03-07:00","id":1137775,"title":"","content":"Termana and Creature Collection III were standouts for me. I loved them both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T14:41:47-07:00","id":1137834,"title":"","content":"I am quite fond of the first Relics &amp; Rituals. The game balance was perhaps not the best, but I really like all the small stories/legends that were attached to each spells/magic items, that made the setting feel alive for me ^^<br /> <br /> I was very impressed by the Termana sourcebook, and I really loved Hollowfaust too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T16:04:01-07:00","id":1137856,"title":"","content":"Hollowfaust was my favorite. Followed by Creature Collection 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T20:43:20-07:00","id":1137908,"title":"","content":"The (revised) Creature Collection holds a special place in my memory because it was the first Scarred Lands book I ever got my hands on.<br /> <br /> But I think my favorite of the old books might just be Edge of Infinity. Most D&amp;D settings tell you about the material world in heavy focus and barely mention anything about other dimensions/planes of existence (and many of them actually share the same set of other planes), so this book really set the Scarred Lands apart from the rest of the crowd, and inspired the high-level portions of many of my campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T05:38:25-07:00","id":1137989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1137648-favorite-old-scarred-lands-books?p=1137834#post1137834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am quite fond of the first Relics &amp; Rituals. The game balance was perhaps not the best, but I really like all the small stories/legends that were attached to each spells/magic items, that made the setting feel alive for me ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Boy howdy was it ever not balanced... but man it was fun. Even though they were sometimes sub-optimal, I always had a soft spot for the Body of Corean spells (the 5 that when you cast them automatically created a new Armor of Light spell on you).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:53:35-07:00","id":1139780,"title":"","content":"R&amp;R II<br /> R&amp;R <br /> Faithful and the forsaken<br /> Hollowfaust<br /> Players guide to wizards bards and sorcerers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/398-rat_bastard","name":"rat_bastard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:23:11-07:00","id":1143943,"title":"","content":"Faithful and the Forsaken: This was a great book for fleshing out the elves and charduni in Termana (especially in a post-resurrection of the dead elven god setting)... but man, I wish we had gotten more than just this and Blood Bayou/Termana hardcover (both very good) for Termana!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}